I want him to have a
good taste in his mouth.

00:52:55.850 --> 00:52:56.820
And then I kind of see that he's just

00:52:56.820 --> 00:52:58.756
sort of sitting outside of the water

00:52:58.756 --> 00:52:59.676
and sitting on the beach.

00:52:59.676 --> 00:53:01.630
So I'm like, I go back in,
I haven't caught any waves,

00:53:01.630 --> 00:53:05.740
I've like totally wiped
out a couple of times

00:53:05.740 --> 00:53:08.070
just 'cause the waves were
unpredictable and it just...

00:53:08.070 --> 00:53:10.790
I wasn't having a good
time, Locke wasn't having

00:53:10.790 --> 00:53:13.500
a good time, Shepherded had quit.

00:53:13.500 --> 00:53:16.390
So I like go and I'm like
trying to help Shepherd

00:53:16.390 --> 00:53:17.360
by like taking him out there

00:53:17.360 --> 00:53:18.980
and pushing him into the waves.

00:53:18.980 --> 00:53:23.730
But the undertow or the
sidetow was so intense

00:53:23.730 --> 00:53:25.197
that I could barely stay with him.

00:53:25.197 --> 00:53:27.370
And I was like, "Man, did we pick a bad?"

00:53:27.370 --> 00:53:29.760
Oh, the beach was rocky.

00:53:29.760 --> 00:53:30.697
- Yeah.

00:53:30.697 --> 00:53:33.180
- And I'm like barefoot,
I didn't bring my booties

00:53:33.180 --> 00:53:35.330
and I was like in the water
like stepping on rocks

00:53:35.330 --> 00:53:38.180
and like my feet hurt
and of course you're cold

00:53:38.180 --> 00:53:40.180
because, you know, it's California.

00:53:40.180 --> 00:53:41.530
- This is not looking good, Rhett.

00:53:41.530 --> 00:53:43.177
- And so this is day one and I'm like,

00:53:43.177 --> 00:53:46.710
"Oh man, is this, I knew
this was gonna happen.

00:53:46.710 --> 00:53:48.490
I knew that the surfing
wasn't gonna be good."

00:53:48.490 --> 00:53:49.760
I started saying things like that.

00:53:49.760 --> 00:53:53.300
Like, "You've always got
your expectations set so high

00:53:53.300 --> 00:53:55.436
for how things are gonna go
and how things are gonna be.

00:53:55.436 --> 00:53:57.120
You're not, you know, I
brought my regular surfboard

00:53:57.120 --> 00:53:59.220
and you're finally gonna be
able to do regular surfing

00:53:59.220 --> 00:54:00.840
and not just stand up paddle boarding.

00:54:00.840 --> 00:54:02.670
And the boys are gonna get good at it."

00:54:02.670 --> 00:54:04.000
You know.

00:54:04.000 --> 00:54:05.350
None of that was happening.

00:54:06.270 --> 00:54:09.420
And so we kind of go inside
a little bit defeated

00:54:10.440 --> 00:54:14.210
and then the next day rolls
around and there was a part

00:54:14.210 --> 00:54:15.390
of me that was just like, "You know what,

00:54:15.390 --> 00:54:16.840
maybe you shouldn't force it.

00:54:17.690 --> 00:54:19.540
You shouldn't force it on yourself.

00:54:19.540 --> 00:54:21.043
Don't force it on your kids.

00:54:22.160 --> 00:54:26.540
Just, just, just vacate."

00:54:26.540 --> 00:54:28.090
Is that how you do vacation?

00:54:28.090 --> 00:54:28.923
You vacate?

00:54:28.923 --> 00:54:29.817
- Yeah, definitely.

00:54:29.817 --> 00:54:33.730
- "Just continue vacating and
don't worry about surfing.

00:54:33.730 --> 00:54:35.147
If it happens, it happens."

00:54:36.940 --> 00:54:39.270
So I'm kind of sitting
up there in the condo,

00:54:39.270 --> 00:54:44.250
I can see the ocean and I can see some,

00:54:44.250 --> 00:54:45.680
it's like mid-morning the next day

00:54:45.680 --> 00:54:48.163
and I see some, and like
I didn't get up and go,

00:54:49.040 --> 00:54:51.810
I see some guys on paddle boards
which I hadn't seen before

00:54:51.810 --> 00:54:55.830
and they're kind of like
getting some waves and stuff.

00:54:55.830 --> 00:54:56.663
- Mm-hmm.

00:54:56.663 --> 00:54:59.140
- And they, I can tell that they're old.

00:54:59.140 --> 00:55:00.640
- Nice.
- Right.

00:55:00.640 --> 00:55:02.010
And I'm kind of in that age group.

00:55:02.010 --> 00:55:05.340
But these guys are like 60s, gray hairs.

00:55:05.340 --> 00:55:07.253
I mean, not that that makes you 60s.

00:55:08.090 --> 00:55:10.520
But these guys were old.

00:55:10.520 --> 00:55:12.750
And, I mean even white hairs.

00:55:12.750 --> 00:55:16.630
And they are kind of killing it out there.

00:55:16.630 --> 00:55:19.400
So I'm like, "Screw it, I'm going."

00:55:19.400 --> 00:55:22.130
But I'm not gonna, I'm not
gonna ask the kids to go

00:55:22.130 --> 00:55:23.350
unless they wanna go.

00:55:23.350 --> 00:55:27.640
So I go down the steps, paddle out there,

00:55:27.640 --> 00:55:29.790
paddle, I'm like paddling
around these old guys,

00:55:29.790 --> 00:55:31.370
I'm like, it is a little bit calmer today,

00:55:31.370 --> 00:55:33.720
like it wasn't so hard
to get out, that's nice.

00:55:35.720 --> 00:55:36.947
And I'm like talking to one of the guys,

00:55:36.947 --> 00:55:37.780
"Catching anything?"

00:55:37.780 --> 00:55:38.613
He's like, "Oh, yeah.

00:55:38.613 --> 00:55:40.890
Every couple of minutes
something comes along."

00:55:40.890 --> 00:55:42.610
Oh, I wasn't like, "Yeah,
I've been watching you

00:55:42.610 --> 00:55:43.727
from my porch."

00:55:45.950 --> 00:55:50.950
And then I start noticing
that the dolphins are out.

00:55:51.030 --> 00:55:52.550
- The dolphins.

00:55:52.550 --> 00:55:57.550
- And they're not just out,
they're like putting on a show.

00:55:59.119 --> 00:55:59.952
- What?

00:55:59.952 --> 00:56:00.850
What do you mean?

00:56:00.850 --> 00:56:01.710
- Well-

00:56:01.710 --> 00:56:02.930
- Hoops? Fire?

00:56:02.930 --> 00:56:05.730
- Two and three dolphins
at a time like are,

00:56:05.730 --> 00:56:07.210
they're swimming in these little pods

00:56:07.210 --> 00:56:09.877
and he, one of the old guys was like,

00:56:09.877 --> 00:56:11.890
"Yeah the dolphins are
really feeding today."

00:56:11.890 --> 00:56:14.720
They're like, you know,
'cause they're like literally

00:56:14.720 --> 00:56:18.210
like swimming a couple
of feet away from you

00:56:18.210 --> 00:56:19.740
and they're like going under
your board and then coming up

00:56:19.740 --> 00:56:20.690
on the other side and stuff.

00:56:20.690 --> 00:56:21.620
They know that you're there.
- It's amazing.

00:56:21.620 --> 00:56:22.670
- Right?
- Oh, yeah.

00:56:23.650 --> 00:56:26.900
- And they know that you're
another intelligent being

00:56:26.900 --> 00:56:30.273
and they know that you're
into watching cool things.

00:56:31.820 --> 00:56:32.653
And so-

00:56:32.653 --> 00:56:33.840
- You think they're doing it for you?

00:56:33.840 --> 00:56:34.955
- No, I think they're doing it

00:56:34.955 --> 00:56:37.040
because they're just expressing themselves

00:56:37.040 --> 00:56:39.490
but they also know that it's cool.

00:56:39.490 --> 00:56:41.630
I mean their brains are bigger than ours.

00:56:41.630 --> 00:56:42.801
- Yeah.

00:56:42.801 --> 00:56:45.300
- They'd be, if they had
thumbs they'd be in charge.

00:56:45.300 --> 00:56:47.060
- Well if they had thumbs
then they'd have hands

00:56:47.060 --> 00:56:48.360
and that would look weird.

00:56:49.730 --> 00:56:52.280
- They wouldn't be nearly
as agile if they had thumbs,

00:56:52.280 --> 00:56:53.373
I do realize that.

00:56:53.373 --> 00:56:54.300
- I don't think they'd be cool.

00:56:54.300 --> 00:56:55.383
And they would know it.

00:56:55.383 --> 00:57:00.383
- Then one of them jumps
completely out of the water.

00:57:01.597 --> 00:57:02.910
- No, I've never seen this.

00:57:02.910 --> 00:57:04.610
- I've never seen this
other than at SeaWorld,

00:57:04.610 --> 00:57:05.720
which we don't go to anymore

00:57:05.720 --> 00:57:07.750
because they don't treat them-

00:57:07.750 --> 00:57:09.470
- Completely out of the water?

00:57:09.470 --> 00:57:13.190
- Total dolphin body two
feet out of the water.

00:57:13.190 --> 00:57:17.031
Head to tail complete out of the water.

00:57:17.031 --> 00:57:18.324
- Whoa.

00:57:18.324 --> 00:57:19.157
What?

00:57:19.157 --> 00:57:20.150
- 20 feet away.

00:57:20.150 --> 00:57:20.983
- Wow.

00:57:20.983 --> 00:57:22.910
- And I'm like, "Oh yeah."

00:57:22.910 --> 00:57:23.930
And then-

00:57:23.930 --> 00:57:25.550
- Did you have a tear?

00:57:25.550 --> 00:57:27.680
- No, I was just like, I'm...

00:57:27.680 --> 00:57:32.680
I said out loud to myself,
"Always choose the experience."

00:57:33.540 --> 00:57:34.373
- Yeah.
- That's, you know,

00:57:34.373 --> 00:57:37.660
I was just reminding myself
I was like, "This is it, man.

00:57:37.660 --> 00:57:40.110
I know it's hard, you're
not a great surfer,

00:57:40.110 --> 00:57:43.000
you're frustrated, you're
kind of out of shape

00:57:43.000 --> 00:57:45.490
and you're tall and I know
you don't have great balance

00:57:45.490 --> 00:57:48.150
but look, you're out here
and look what's happening.

00:57:48.150 --> 00:57:50.707
The dolphins are putting on a free show."

00:57:51.550 --> 00:57:52.680
Then-
- Yeah.

00:57:52.680 --> 00:57:56.780
- There's a, a one dolphin that
was a little more weathered

00:57:57.720 --> 00:57:58.680
than the other ones.

00:57:58.680 --> 00:58:03.050
He looked older and darker and more worn.

00:58:03.050 --> 00:58:04.030
- Okay.

00:58:04.030 --> 00:58:07.330
- I notice that every time
he comes up, he's snorting.

00:58:07.330 --> 00:58:08.450
Like (snorting).

00:58:08.450 --> 00:58:09.750
Like there was blow hole.

00:58:09.750 --> 00:58:12.010
His blow hole's making a lot of noise.

00:58:12.010 --> 00:58:13.233
- What?

00:58:13.233 --> 00:58:15.600
- And I don't know if he
was doing it to be cool

00:58:15.600 --> 00:58:18.740
or if it's just a condition
but I appreciated it.

00:58:18.740 --> 00:58:19.573
It was like, "Wow.

00:58:19.573 --> 00:58:22.350
I mean this guy's making all this noise."

00:58:22.350 --> 00:58:24.020
You know, none of, the
rest of them are jumping

00:58:24.020 --> 00:58:26.980
and doing things but this guy
he's making a lot of noise.

00:58:26.980 --> 00:58:27.890
- Dad grunting.

00:58:27.890 --> 00:58:29.914
- Yeah, and I appreciated that.

00:58:29.914 --> 00:58:31.160
And then-

00:58:31.160 --> 00:58:32.420
- That's wild.

00:58:32.420 --> 00:58:37.420
- And then, a wave comes and I'm like...

00:58:38.060 --> 00:58:40.580
Now I had tried to catch a
couple of waves and again-

00:58:40.580 --> 00:58:42.670
- You were putting on a
show for the dolphins.

00:58:42.670 --> 00:58:45.300
- Again, it's complicated.

00:58:45.300 --> 00:58:47.380
Do you know how when you're
out, I'm out pretty far,

00:58:47.380 --> 00:58:50.410
I'm out several hundred yards, you know?

00:58:50.410 --> 00:58:52.130
I'm way out in the ocean.

00:58:52.130 --> 00:58:52.963
- Uh-huh.

00:58:52.963 --> 00:58:55.130
- Because the way that the waves work

00:58:55.130 --> 00:58:57.590
at this particular beach,
it's a beach break,

00:58:57.590 --> 00:59:02.590
is there's, waves of a
certain size break out there

00:59:04.050 --> 00:59:07.850
and then they, so they
break and there's whitewater

00:59:07.850 --> 00:59:10.150
and then they kind of stop
and then they reform early,

00:59:10.150 --> 00:59:11.840
you know, further inside.

00:59:11.840 --> 00:59:12.673
- Mm-hmm.

00:59:12.673 --> 00:59:14.490
- But you want to be out there,
especially on a paddleboard,

00:59:14.490 --> 00:59:16.500
because you don't wanna
have to get through

00:59:16.500 --> 00:59:17.333
those every time.

00:59:17.333 --> 00:59:19.370
So you're actually kind
of surfing these waves

00:59:19.370 --> 00:59:21.370
on a first break way out there

00:59:21.370 --> 00:59:24.330
and then kind of like as they
kind of dissipate you go back

00:59:24.330 --> 00:59:25.163
out and you...

00:59:25.163 --> 00:59:29.070
So you surf and you never
fall off your board,

00:59:29.070 --> 00:59:30.319
you never have to peel out of the wave,

00:59:30.319 --> 00:59:31.450
the wave just kind of dissipates.

00:59:31.450 --> 00:59:34.770
But you get a good like
10, 12 second surf,

00:59:34.770 --> 00:59:35.623
which is awesome.

00:59:36.870 --> 00:59:38.460
And then sometimes if
the wave is big enough

00:59:38.460 --> 00:59:40.360
it will reconstitute
while you're still in it

00:59:40.360 --> 00:59:41.650
and you'll catch the second break

00:59:41.650 --> 00:59:43.024
and take it all the way to the shore.

00:59:43.024 --> 00:59:43.890
Right?

00:59:43.890 --> 00:59:47.260
That did happen one time during the week.

00:59:47.260 --> 00:59:51.670
But anyway, I catch a
wave and like I don't look

00:59:51.670 --> 00:59:54.030
like an idiot and I do it
right and I'm in the pocket

00:59:54.030 --> 00:59:57.750
and I'm like going sideways
and I'm like, "Yeah, dolphins,

00:59:57.750 --> 00:59:59.590
I'm catching the waves."

00:59:59.590 --> 01:00:02.927
And then as I'm paddling
back out there's another wave

01:00:02.927 --> 01:00:06.640
that's coming at me and
I look into the wave

01:00:06.640 --> 01:00:09.966
and there's two dolphins
surfing in the wave.

01:00:09.966 --> 01:00:10.799
- What?

01:00:10.799 --> 01:00:14.740
- Like in, their like
noses are just piercing out

01:00:14.740 --> 01:00:16.297
of the face of the wave and they're like,

01:00:16.297 --> 01:00:18.750
and they go right under my board.

01:00:18.750 --> 01:00:19.583
- Really?

01:00:19.583 --> 01:00:20.416
- Yeah.

01:00:20.416 --> 01:00:22.427
I mean and that's not as cool
as the time I was surfing

01:00:22.427 --> 01:00:24.577
and there were dolphins
on the wave with me

01:00:25.620 --> 01:00:28.917
but I was just like,
"This is why I'm here."

01:00:29.820 --> 01:00:32.350
And then, so that, the
highlight of my trip,

01:00:32.350 --> 01:00:33.770
which, you know, the highlight of my life

01:00:33.770 --> 01:00:35.390
is when I caught a wave and
the dolphins were on it.

01:00:35.390 --> 01:00:38.980
The highlight of my
trip was just out there,

01:00:38.980 --> 01:00:41.610
having chosen the experience,
having a little bit

01:00:41.610 --> 01:00:44.380
of luck with surfing but
experiencing these dolphins.

01:00:44.380 --> 01:00:46.230
- Dang, man, I'm envious.

01:00:46.230 --> 01:00:48.720
- And then at that point I come back

01:00:48.720 --> 01:00:51.340
and I tell my dolphin stories
and that kind of gets the boys

01:00:51.340 --> 01:00:52.830
kind of back into it.

01:00:52.830 --> 01:00:57.653
The rest of the week we went
out once, often twice a day,

01:00:58.530 --> 01:01:00.890
Locke's catching waves,
Shepherd's catching the waves

01:01:00.890 --> 01:01:01.913
on the inside.

01:01:04.460 --> 01:01:09.230
And then the final day I actually met,

01:01:09.230 --> 01:01:12.180
so my therapist lives
close by to this area,

01:01:12.180 --> 01:01:16.040
so I actually had my therapy
appointment on the beach.

01:01:16.040 --> 01:01:18.290
It was the most Southern
California thing ever

01:01:18.290 --> 01:01:20.160
walking with your therapist down the beach

01:01:20.160 --> 01:01:21.763
but I love everything about it.

01:01:24.267 --> 01:01:28.700
And then it was like, "Can't
we have a, can't we make a,

01:01:33.330 --> 01:01:36.480
why can't we surf during
a therapy session?

01:01:36.480 --> 01:01:38.857
I mean, who says we can't do that?"

01:01:41.050 --> 01:01:42.630
So we did.

01:01:42.630 --> 01:01:43.463
- Okay.

01:01:43.463 --> 01:01:46.900
- And Locke came out, and this was a sun,

01:01:46.900 --> 01:01:51.900
it was literally watching
the sunset while surfing

01:01:53.290 --> 01:01:57.450
like saw the sun go over
the horizon while surfing

01:01:57.450 --> 01:02:02.450
and then big wave came, me
and Locke catch it together

01:02:04.730 --> 01:02:06.240
and I'm like, "Party wave."

01:02:06.240 --> 01:02:08.480
You always gotta say
party wave when two people

01:02:08.480 --> 01:02:09.313
catch a wave.

01:02:09.313 --> 01:02:11.810
And like, we're like, boards
are like two feet apart

01:02:11.810 --> 01:02:16.640
and we're like big wave,
flying on this wave,

01:02:16.640 --> 01:02:20.040
and I'm like, he, you know,
we're both regular footers

01:02:20.040 --> 01:02:21.440
so he's in front of me so he can't see me,

01:02:21.440 --> 01:02:23.280
I'm like yelling at him just
to make sure he understands

01:02:23.280 --> 01:02:24.450
that we're on this wave
together and he's like looking

01:02:24.450 --> 01:02:27.910
back at me and then like
he totally wipes out

01:02:27.910 --> 01:02:28.743
right in front of me.

01:02:28.743 --> 01:02:30.870
But after we had surfed
for a good 10 seconds.

01:02:30.870 --> 01:02:32.890
I mean it was like we
got, we caught this wave,

01:02:32.890 --> 01:02:34.730
it was great.

01:02:34.730 --> 01:02:35.563
And then that was it.

01:02:35.563 --> 01:02:36.396
That was the last.

01:02:36.396 --> 01:02:38.670
I was so tired after that I didn't surf

01:02:38.670 --> 01:02:41.637
the morning of the last
day it was just like,

01:02:41.637 --> 01:02:43.650
"Boy, I'm out of shape."

01:02:43.650 --> 01:02:47.040
But I had some special moments.

01:02:47.040 --> 01:02:48.120
- That's amazing, man.

01:02:48.120 --> 01:02:49.210
- Special moments.

01:02:49.210 --> 01:02:52.223
- I'm so mad that it was you and not me.

01:02:54.710 --> 01:02:55.882
- Yeah.

01:02:55.882 --> 01:02:57.650
I mean, and also it just
reminded me is like we gotta,

01:02:57.650 --> 01:02:59.050
I mean we gotta get back out there.

01:02:59.050 --> 01:03:02.610
We gotta get back out there
on a more regular basis.

01:03:02.610 --> 01:03:04.410
It's just, you know, we're so far...

01:03:05.692 --> 01:03:07.593
We're so far, I mean an hour.

01:03:08.510 --> 01:03:10.270
People don't realize
how big Los Angeles is.

01:03:10.270 --> 01:03:11.560
We're like an hour from the beach.

01:03:11.560 --> 01:03:12.393
- [Link] Yeah.

01:03:13.380 --> 01:03:15.480
- So you kind of have
to make plans for it.

01:03:15.480 --> 01:03:17.430
- But I do, I love the principle

01:03:17.430 --> 01:03:22.430
of like as often as possible
say yes to the experience.

01:03:25.760 --> 01:03:26.593
I love that.

01:03:26.593 --> 01:03:27.430
I love that.

01:03:27.430 --> 01:03:30.310
Now it's your, it's your week for the rec.

01:03:30.310 --> 01:03:31.143
- Oh.

01:03:31.143 --> 01:03:31.976
- So...

01:03:33.250 --> 01:03:34.190
- Say yes to the experience.

01:03:34.190 --> 01:03:35.730
- I want to get your, get your rec,

01:03:35.730 --> 01:03:37.400
but, you know, one of the
things you talked about

01:03:37.400 --> 01:03:40.440
I think, I can, since
we kind of planned out

01:03:40.440 --> 01:03:42.190
what we're gonna talk about
for the next "Ear Biscuit"

01:03:42.190 --> 01:03:43.810
we can give a teaser.

01:03:43.810 --> 01:03:46.120
You know, we were talking
about Lily at the top

01:03:46.120 --> 01:03:50.860
and talking about the mentality
of coming out of COVID

01:03:50.860 --> 01:03:53.040
and like the things you
find yourself thinking

